{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md && cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md && cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md && cat README.md && cat specification/INTENT.md && cat specification/PRODUCT.md && cat specification/GOALS.md && cat specification/REQUIREMENT.md && cat design/DESIGN.md && cat .qualification/OWNER.json && cat .qualification/ROOT-OWNER.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md && cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md && cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md && cat README.md && cat specification/INTENT.md && cat specification/PRODUCT.md && cat specification/GOALS.md && cat specification/REQUIREMENT.md && cat design/DESIGN.md && cat .qualification/OWNER.json && cat .qualification/ROOT-OWNER.json'","aggregated_output":"# Bounded handoff and independent review\n\nUse delegation only when required by a material boundary and authorized by the current configuration. A sufficient direct Writer task goes straight from current basis/grant to the exact effect and focused proof; no automatic coordination or review gate is added.\n\nBefore handoff retain:\n- Exact outcome and subject; Product Definition and immutable method; governing requirement and design; changed producer, transport, consumer and artifact relations.\n- Frame id/revision and result algebra; activation identity; operation grant and precise territory; separate semantic, evaluation, decision, acceptance and publication authorities.\n- Required evidence and predicates; admissible source routes; retained failures/counterexamples; original observations and their provenance.\n- Host/tool implementation and method support; actor/context/resource limits and exclusions; stop/change invalidators; return schema and named consumer.\n\nSelect only the smallest dependency-ready reference frontier that preserves those distinctions. If it does not fit the envelope, refine or sequence within existing authority; seek the actual missing capability or envelope decision when needed. Do not erase material obligations to fit.\n\nDiscover the supported `context.assemble`, `contract.preflight`, `dispatch.start`, `dispatch.observe`, `return.capture` and `return.check` contracts through the public path in [tools](tools.md), selecting only operations required by this activation. A missing supported binding stops the dependent handoff. Do not replace the selected dispatch with a native spawn just because it exists. Retain the actual input delivery, process result, stdout/stderr and parsed original closed return. Transport success and actor output availability do not establish requested effects or fitness.\n\nWorkers implement only their grant, self-assess the exact candidate and return. They do not activate the next stage. Executive consumes closed results and selects only an already authorized next action; if a record must be written, bind a Writer rather than mutating in the Executive frame.\n\nA required Reviewer acquires governing sources and derives expected behavior before the exact candidate and proof. Use a fresh permitted reviewer and retain actual exposure, author relationship, model family/resolution and limitations. Nonauthor same-family review does not prove cross-family independence. Where a review.prepare tool is selected, actually call its supported contract. The Reviewer reports findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty; it does not implement the adopted repair or decide promotion. After material repair, withdraw only affected old reliance and obtain the required fresh assessment.\n\nA returned candidate_ready concerns availability. Assessments keep their own predicates and results. Owner disposition is a separate act. Contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting.\n# Bind the exact workspace and method\n\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n\n```sh\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n```\n\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n|---|---|\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n# Public tool path\n\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n\n```sh\n\"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n  --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\nJSON\n```\n\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\n```json\n{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n```\nUse operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n\nFor an authorized write:\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n\nFor `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\ncat: README.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
