{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"stdo_q05","tool":"source.read","arguments":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"exec-stage1-governing-8","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"standards/EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[177,248]},"sha256":"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff"},"encoding":"utf8"}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:eed94ef64aaf93b05ee465457ee4eda6370316167d5b8bd0aabe1216fea6f5b2\",\"sha256\":\"eed94ef64aaf93b05ee465457ee4eda6370316167d5b8bd0aabe1216fea6f5b2\"},\"id\":\"exec-stage1-governing-8\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=79a373d2f5a3b767880d05b6a3a5df1c5420a85019badc04d2cd7a1479343628]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 3. Independent assessment\\n\\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law).\\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\\na governing basis may add boundaries.\\n\\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\\nof its run, which\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (P6).\\n\\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\\nthe other (P6, P3).\\n\\nReporting a defect, supplying a counterexample or identifying behaviour\\nalready required by governing law does not by itself author the realised\\nsubject. Contributing wording, design or policy that is adopted into the\\nsubject, including through directions for a particular repair, is authorship\\nof that contribution. A\\nreporter may assess a later repair only when the existing assessment grant,\\nauthorship relation and evidence-independence conditions permit it; a\\nreporter gains no review authority from having found the defect. A person\\nwho authored an adopted repair cannot supply its required independent\\nassessment by calling that authorship a finding (P6, P3).\\n\\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6;\\n[TICKETS UP-007](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007)). A contribution received from another author stays that\\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\\n\\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\\nstated is that they are not independent.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[177,248]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff\",\"selected_sha256\":\"d5e8cd4f574cebc1728e1aefafd5cd05763ab782f872bce3f29d7c8649e442c9\",\"size_bytes\":4472,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[177,248]},\"sha256\":\"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}],"structured_content":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:eed94ef64aaf93b05ee465457ee4eda6370316167d5b8bd0aabe1216fea6f5b2","sha256":"eed94ef64aaf93b05ee465457ee4eda6370316167d5b8bd0aabe1216fea6f5b2"},"id":"exec-stage1-governing-8","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=79a373d2f5a3b767880d05b6a3a5df1c5420a85019badc04d2cd7a1479343628]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 3. Independent assessment\n\nA constructor's self-review is construction output, not assessment. Where\npromotion needs independent assessment, the assessor evaluates the exact\nlive subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the\nconstructor's summary (P6, and P0 with its premise that a step's output is\na candidate until evaluated; instance premise (c) of §1 Foundation to law).\nThis section decides what counts as independent assessment. Which\nboundaries require it is a policy choice of the Spec Method, owned by\n[TICKETS §7 Execution and verification authority separation](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007);\na governing basis may add boundaries.\n\nProtocol: where method qualification applies\n([§7 Method self-qualification](#method-self-qualification)), the subject is\nfrozen by identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere it is\nstabilised by an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation\nsufficient for the claimed assessment. The assessor records its\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\nown authorship. Reusing the constructor's judgment does not satisfy\nindependence; shared mechanical evidence may be reused, judgment may not\n(ACTIVATION §7). Binding a returned assessment to its producer, subject,\nbasis and evidence authenticates the result; it establishes neither the\nassertion provenance of its expected answer nor the execution provenance\nof its run, which\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance)\nrequires separately (P6, P3). Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results));\nno cryptographic or transport protocol is prescribed for the binding (P6). Any post-exposure revision is a declared intervention: it\nis either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new\nqualification subject, and it cannot retroactively make the original\nfrozen construction pass. This law prescribes no actor type or count,\nreview-round count, engine, prompt or orchestration (P6).\n\nAuthor identity is the party responsible for the content of a realised\nsubject. It is distinct from actor identity, whoever performs one\noperation, which is an identity and not an authority\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)).\nAuthorship is one of the conditions on\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\nthe other (P6, P3).\n\nReporting a defect, supplying a counterexample or identifying behaviour\nalready required by governing law does not by itself author the realised\nsubject. Contributing wording, design or policy that is adopted into the\nsubject, including through directions for a particular repair, is authorship\nof that contribution. A\nreporter may assess a later repair only when the existing assessment grant,\nauthorship relation and evidence-independence conditions permit it; a\nreporter gains no review authority from having found the defect. A person\nwho authored an adopted repair cannot supply its required independent\nassessment by calling that authorship a finding (P6, P3).\n\nIndependence rests on authorship and on the evidence conditions above, not\non a new context. The assessor may read the same governing sources as the\nconstructor. A fresh context alone establishes no independence, and it\nsupplies no review authority the author lacks: an author that opens a\nfresh context to review its own candidate is still its author, and its\nreview is self-review, which stays construction output and cannot be\nrelabelled as independent assessment (P6;\n[TICKETS UP-007](TICKETS.md#execution-and-verification-authority-separation-up-007)). A contribution received from another author stays that\nauthor's wherever it is carried, and that author's reading of it supplies\nno independent acceptance of it (P6).\n\nIndependence across actor families is declared, not assumed. Whether two\nactivations of one model family are independent for a semantic judgment is a\npolicy the governing basis states for the claim; the default where it is not\nstated is that they are not independent.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[177,248]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff","selected_sha256":"d5e8cd4f574cebc1728e1aefafd5cd05763ab782f872bce3f29d7c8649e442c9","size_bytes":4472,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"standards/EVALUATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[177,248]},"sha256":"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
