{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"stdo_q05","tool":"source.read","arguments":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"exec-stage1-contract-source-2","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","root":"method","path":"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md","object":null,"sha256":"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e","selector":{"lines":[535,578]}},"encoding":"utf8"}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:4f0997e3c7dcec044f501c986abf5fe631d47f4af0aa65f6ff925b3da40d8d95\",\"sha256\":\"4f0997e3c7dcec044f501c986abf5fe631d47f4af0aa65f6ff925b3da40d8d95\"},\"id\":\"exec-stage1-contract-source-2\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d8dd52a042b98e30defc940a3f377d8f8d791a27b23d14df0d4ad1a1ae7628ba]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 6. Executive attention, evaluation and action\\n\\n### The three duties\\n\\nThe Executive is the frame for three inseparable duties over one governed\\noutcome (P0, P6, P2):\\n\\n1. attention management: it keeps the exact outcome and basis, the\\n   Product-role map, the evaluation inventory, the dependency relation, the\\n   unresolved frontier, the actor envelopes, the current MVP or release\\n   mandate, the applicable triage policy and the residual boundary, and it\\n   selects the smallest dependency-ready activation set sufficient for the\\n   next decision within the finite actor envelopes;\\n2. evaluation orchestration: it activates capable Workers, Reviewers or\\n   specialists, keeps their exact subjects and bases, and consumes only\\n   closed results or declared translations; and\\n3. authorised action selection: it assigns priority, determines the effect\\n   on the current promotion boundary, applies an existing disposition, and\\n   issues only the next already-authorised activation or action.\\n\\nThe Executive does not contain the complete workspace and does not perform\\nevery evaluation. It acquires no Product meaning, implementation, mutation,\\nacceptance, publication or other operation authority from the role. A\\nmaterial effect stays owned by the actor that carries its exact operation\\ngrant (P6, RF-002).\\n\\n### No mutation while Executive\\n\\nAn actor occupying the Executive frame modifies no candidate, Product or\\nworktree bytes and performs no implementation effect. Filesystem or tool\\naccess is no exception, and neither is an edit that is small, test-only,\\nreversible or apparently obvious. Mutation requires a separately activated\\nWorker or Writer relation carrying the exact operation grant, subject and\\nwrite territory. A same-actor role transition is explicit and is recorded in\\nthe existing work carrier before the effect; for that effect the actor is no\\nlonger acting as Executive. Recording or delegating after an Executive edit\\ncannot authorise the edit retroactively (P6, P3). This prohibition is this\\nprofile's, and it applies wherever the executive configuration is selected\\n([ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration), Example; §7);\\nan operation grant covering a construction, status and checkpoint sequence\\ndoes not lift it\\n([ACTIVATION §1 Roles and delegation](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation)).\\n\\n### Attention cycle\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[535,578]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e\",\"selected_sha256\":\"94ae5ca9bd7a731e18abad945f378cf460fe0e1ed2a2d828bf0b2033870b22b8\",\"size_bytes\":2358,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[535,578]},\"sha256\":\"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}],"structured_content":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:4f0997e3c7dcec044f501c986abf5fe631d47f4af0aa65f6ff925b3da40d8d95","sha256":"4f0997e3c7dcec044f501c986abf5fe631d47f4af0aa65f6ff925b3da40d8d95"},"id":"exec-stage1-contract-source-2","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d8dd52a042b98e30defc940a3f377d8f8d791a27b23d14df0d4ad1a1ae7628ba]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 6. Executive attention, evaluation and action\n\n### The three duties\n\nThe Executive is the frame for three inseparable duties over one governed\noutcome (P0, P6, P2):\n\n1. attention management: it keeps the exact outcome and basis, the\n   Product-role map, the evaluation inventory, the dependency relation, the\n   unresolved frontier, the actor envelopes, the current MVP or release\n   mandate, the applicable triage policy and the residual boundary, and it\n   selects the smallest dependency-ready activation set sufficient for the\n   next decision within the finite actor envelopes;\n2. evaluation orchestration: it activates capable Workers, Reviewers or\n   specialists, keeps their exact subjects and bases, and consumes only\n   closed results or declared translations; and\n3. authorised action selection: it assigns priority, determines the effect\n   on the current promotion boundary, applies an existing disposition, and\n   issues only the next already-authorised activation or action.\n\nThe Executive does not contain the complete workspace and does not perform\nevery evaluation. It acquires no Product meaning, implementation, mutation,\nacceptance, publication or other operation authority from the role. A\nmaterial effect stays owned by the actor that carries its exact operation\ngrant (P6, RF-002).\n\n### No mutation while Executive\n\nAn actor occupying the Executive frame modifies no candidate, Product or\nworktree bytes and performs no implementation effect. Filesystem or tool\naccess is no exception, and neither is an edit that is small, test-only,\nreversible or apparently obvious. Mutation requires a separately activated\nWorker or Writer relation carrying the exact operation grant, subject and\nwrite territory. A same-actor role transition is explicit and is recorded in\nthe existing work carrier before the effect; for that effect the actor is no\nlonger acting as Executive. Recording or delegating after an Executive edit\ncannot authorise the edit retroactively (P6, P3). This prohibition is this\nprofile's, and it applies wherever the executive configuration is selected\n([ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration), Example; §7);\nan operation grant covering a construction, status and checkpoint sequence\ndoes not lift it\n([ACTIVATION §1 Roles and delegation](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation)).\n\n### Attention cycle\n","coordinates":{"lines":[535,578]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e","selected_sha256":"94ae5ca9bd7a731e18abad945f378cf460fe0e1ed2a2d828bf0b2033870b22b8","size_bytes":2358,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[535,578]},"sha256":"fcef434630e270d216f494de97ee727ad46690db89a4b73edac4b88ff921c62e"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
